            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.9 (build 886)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Settings &#8250; Deliveries.</b> The services on this Mac &#8212; Suite, Google Drive, Dropbox, Box, Frame.io Drive &#8212; each with where a delivery goes as a <b>template</b> with tokens ({job}, {date}, {review}, {client}, {show}) and a live preview; <b>Learn from a Folder&#8230;</b> derives the template from one example delivery folder; the studio&#8217;s layout is the default. The job is read from the clips&#8217; paths, or asked for in one picker when they name none.</li>
<li><b>One stop shop.</b> Asobi installs rclone itself (a pinned release, checksum-checked) and <b>Connect Google Drive&#8230; / Dropbox&#8230; / Box&#8230;</b> signs in through the browser; deliveries then upload straight to the service &#8212; no desktop client needed. Asobi never sees a password or a token.</li>
<li><b>No cross-contamination.</b> A cloud delivery goes only under the one folder the app owns, <b>AsobiReview/</b>, which the app never shares; before every Drive delivery it checks that folder is unshared and refuses if it isn&#8217;t; a link, when the policy allows one, is a reader link for the delivery folder alone, expiring where the service permits. <b>Box never gets a link</b>: invite people in Box as Previewer or Viewer, and review copies are the default for Box.</li>
<li><b>Delete Delivery&#8230;</b> in the Review Manager removes a delivered package from the service so nothing can be downloaded again; the review&#8217;s notes and marks stay. Every delivery is recorded on the review&#8217;s row with its link.</li>
<li>A delivery folder is never overwritten (a re-delivery gets its own), and carries a small record naming its review.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
